    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nI encountered an issue where the cursor's horizontal position is lost after scrolling using C-d / C-u / C-f commands.\r\n\r\nI faced a similar problem with another plugin, which was related to the 'winhl' option in Neovim. A fix for this issue can be found here: [#27470](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/27470). Consequently, I believe this issue might be related.\r\n\r\nI haven't opened an issue on Neovim because I'm unsure about which option is set by this plugin and how exactly the plugin operates or even if the issues are related.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-2445+g2e1f5055a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. this code:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nmkdir repro\r\ncd repro\r\ngit clone https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\r\ncat >repro.lua <<EOF\r\nvim.o.runtimepath = os.getenv('PWD') .. '/mini.nvim,' .. vim.o.runtimepath\r\nrequire('mini.animate').setup()\r\nEOF\r\nnvim --clean -u repro.lua\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. edit a long file that has multiple short and long lines. \r\n3. scroll down by C-d and C-u and the issue will occur.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nkeep cursor column position\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nlose cursor column position",
