            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nWould you mind elaborating a bit about what do you mean by \"cursor column position is lost\"?\r\n\r\nMy current understanding is that if before scroll cursor was on come column (say 20) and after scroll it happens to land on the last column of short line (say 10), then next scroll tries to set cursor on line 10 instead of 20 (even if line is long enough)? If this is the case, then I don't think this is a big issue. I'll take a look at if this can be solved relatively pain free, but I'd not have hopes up (as the only way to use the information about where cursor \"wants\" to go is with Vimscript `getcurpos()` and `cursor()` with which I did not have much success in 'mini.animate').",
