        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thank you for the response.\r\n\r\n> My current understanding is that if before scroll cursor was on come column (say 20) and after scroll it happens to land on the last column of short line (say 10), then next scroll tries to set cursor on line 10 instead of 20 (even if line is long enough)\r\n\r\nYes, this is the issue. I've noticed this especially when it reaches an empty line, column 0, and remains there during scrolling.\r\n\r\nGiven my experience with a similar issue caused by Neovim `options` in another plugin, I raised this concern.\r\n\r\n> If this is the case, then I don't think this is a big issue. I'll take a look at if this can be solved relatively pain free, but I'd not have hopes up\r\n\r\nSince I'm not fully familiar with how the plugin operates, and probably the scrolling is not fully controlled, then there is no issue here.\r\n\r\nThank you",
